Z||000000||NITTO||07-12-2000||11:21 PM||||Currently looking at purchasing an 88 Fiero GT.   The car is in mint condition with only 30,000 original miles.  The car sat for six years with out being started, when the current owner bought it.  Seals were dried out, but they were replaced.  The only problem he had with the car was a bearing broke in his transmission, is this normal?  The transmission was replaced a few months ago.  This would be my first Fiero and am very excited, but want other’s opinions on this car.  Haven't driven it yet but planning to see it this weekend.||||reg||4
Z||000001||gixxer||07-12-2000||11:41 PM||||A similar situation with my Formula. Time seems to age the rubber front suspension and steering rack bushings. Look in the distributor cap area and clean out any rust, or replace(probably the original cap like mine was). Change the spark plugs. If any of the tires are original, junk them or be prepared for a thrill ride. <BR>Change all the fluids. I think once you do a little sorting out, you'll really like the car!  ||||reg||1
